    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d333">

                <pb facs="0502" n="403" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg403"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">360c.1121 Zarzycki, Stephen/3: Telegram (part
                    air)</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Poland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Nielsen</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Warsaw</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-07-23T15:00:00+01:00">July 23, 1936—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 24—3:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>67. Complied with your telegram of July 18, 3 p.m., in a conversation yesterday
                    with Undersecretary of State.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d333-f1"/> Embassy has this
                    noon been informed by Foreign Office that the Minister for Finance<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d333-f2"/> has called for July 29, and that he will personally
                    preside over a meeting of the chiefs of customs offices from all border
                    stations. Instructions already have been sent to border officials to administer
                    regulations less rigidly.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Nielsen</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d333-f1" n="5" xml:id="d333-f1-content">
                <p>Count Jan Szembek.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d333-f2" n="6" xml:id="d333-f2-content">
                <p>Eugenjusz Kwiatkowski, also Vice Premier.</p>
            </note>
